# qflix-reaper.exclude — items the reaper must NEVER delete, regardless of age.
#
# This is a protect-list: any item matching a line here is skipped even when it
# is over the age threshold. Lenient parse: '#' starts a comment, blank lines are
# ignored, leading/trailing whitespace is stripped. A missing file = no
# exclusions + a logged WARNING (not an error).
#
# Each non-comment line is exactly one of these four forms:
#
#   tmdb:<id>        match a movie by its TMDB id        e.g.  tmdb:603
#   tvdb:<id>        match a series by its TVDB id        e.g.  tvdb:81189
#   plex:<ratingKey> match a Plex item by its ratingKey   e.g.  plex:14823
#   <title text>     bare line = case-insensitive title   e.g.  The Matrix
#
# Prefer tmdb:/tvdb:/plex: forms — they are exact. Bare-title matching is a
# convenience for one-off pins but will exclude EVERY item whose title matches
# case-insensitively, so use it carefully.

# --- examples (delete or replace with your real pins) ---
# tmdb:603
# tvdb:81189
# plex:14823
# Planet Earth II

# The Welcome-library video (operator pin, 2026-08-08). Today this line is
# belt-and-suspenders twice over: the reaper's LIBRARIES allowlist does not
# include "QFlix - Welcome" (section never queried), and the video resolves to
# no *arr record (deletion structurally impossible). The pin exists so that if
# either of those facts ever changes -- Welcome added to LIBRARIES, or the
# video somehow acquiring an *arr id -- the instruction video still cannot age
# out. It is the front door of the membership funnel, not media.
Welcome to QFlix

# REMOVED 2026-09-13 (per-file retention, docs/superpowers/specs/
# 2026-09-12-reaper-d-per-file-retention-spec.md). This pin was a tourniquet
# for the exact defect the per-file rewrite fixes: the reaper graded Futurama
# on the SERIES' Plex container addedAt (1739683831 = 2025-02-16, the day the
# show shell first entered the library), not on when its CURRENT files
# arrived, so every re-acquisition read as 572 days old and was reaped again
# within the hour. R-4 now rejects the container clock outright; grading is
# per EPISODE FILE against the Plex leaf addedAt corroborated by Sonarr's own
# episodeFile.dateAdded (R-1/R-2). Futurama is also `continuing`
# (ended=false), so its series record is additionally covered by the
# `permanent` tag policy (P-3, scripts/maint/qflix-permanent.py) once tagged.
# The regression this pin stood in for is now a permanent hermetic test:
# tests/unit/test_qflix_reaper.py::test_futurama_regression_container_addedat_never_graded.
